## Context

The observatory's documents come from bounded collection rounds. New JETP
documents (plans, progress reports, project pages, news) appear weekly, and
nothing watches for them between rounds. Tracker [[0715]] puts source watching
in M2, after M1b ([[0833]]); [[0722]] installs the skill and rules that the
refresh follows. This ticket is the recurring run itself.

What already exists:
- `scripts/jetp/build_source_sweep.py` and `scripts/jetp/_source_watch.py`
  record a sweep: checks, discoveries (`new_candidate`, `changed`,
  `checked_no_change`, `blocked`, `error`, `partial`), acquisitions and a
  change report. Every discovery stays an `unadmitted_candidate`; the module
  has no publication operation and never edits the registry.
- The `jetp-research` skill carries the search method and source hierarchy.

## Author decisions (2026-09-25)

- A **local agent** runs the search, not a hosted Claude or Codex session.
- It belongs to the M2 train.

## Design constraints

- Frequency: weekly is the working assumption (JETP news moves by the week;
  daily would mostly find nothing). The author may change it.
- Output: a source-sweep file in the existing contract, proposed as a PR
  for the author to triage. The agent never admits a document, never runs
  `dvc push`, never publishes (same invariant as [[0722]]).
- Runs in a dedicated persistent checkout on padme, shared with the monthly
  link check of [[1141]], never in the author's primary checkout.
- Secrets per `.claude/rules/keystore.md`: read at use, never logged.

## Open questions for the pilot

- Runtime and model: padme runs `llama-server.service` (llama.cpp, system
  service, user haduong) serving Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M with its mmproj on
  `127.0.0.1:8080`, context 131072, all layers on the GPUs (RTX A4000 16 GB +
  RTX 3060 12 GB; 125 GB RAM). Checked 2026-09-25. Its command line shows no
  `--jinja`, which llama.cpp needs for OpenAI-style tool calling: confirm, then
  check that the model follows the skill's tool loop well enough. The agent
  harness that drives the model (tool loop, fetch, file writes) is still to
  choose.
- Web search: a local model has no search of its own. Candidates: a
  self-hosted metasearch (SearXNG), a search API with a key in the keystore,
  or a fixed watch list of source pages (the source universe of [[0715]])
  checked for changes, with open search only as a second pass.
- Quality bar: the pilot compares one week of local-agent candidates for one
  country against a hosted-agent run of the `jetp-research` skill on the same
  week, and reports recall and false positives before the schedule is turned on.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Pilot on one country: local-agent sweep vs hosted-agent sweep, recall and false positives reported, author accepts the bar
- [ ] Weekly schedule on padme in the shared persistent checkout, output as a source-sweep PR, nothing admitted automatically
- [ ] A run that finds nothing, or fails, says so in its log; a silent run is not an all-clear
- [ ] Runbook in `deliverables/jetp-observatory/README.md` (or the refresh skill of [[0722]])
